def pv_print(resfile=None, restype=None, nconting=None, contingarray=None, noutputs=None, outputsarray=None, interface=None, enforcescale=None, uselinestyles=None, numberlines=None, prtparams=None, **kwds):
    """
Use this API to print the results of PV analysis from the file.

Python syntax:

pv_print(resfile, restype, nconting, contingarray, noutputs, outputsarray, interface, enforcescale, uselinestyles, numberlines, prtparams)

where:

Character RESFILE*260  Is the name of the existing *.pv file.
Integer RESTYPE  Type of the results. The values are as follows:
RESTYPE = 0 bus voltage
RESTYPE = 1 generator MW
RESTYPE = 2 branch MVA flow
RESTYPE = 3 interface MW flow
RESTYPE = 4 bus voltage against interface flow.
Integer NCONTING  Number of specified contingencies.
Integer CONTINGARRAY(NCONTING)  Is an array of the numbers of specified contingencies. The base case is marked by 0. The size of the array is equal to NCONTING.
Integer NOUTPUTS  Number of specified outputs.
Integer OUTPUTSARRAY(NOUTPUTS)  Is an array of the numbers of specified outputs. The count starts from 0. The size of the array is equal to NOUTPUTS.
Integer INTERFACE  Number of specified interface. Valid only in case of bus voltage against interface flow (RESTYPE = 4).
Integer ENFORCESCALE  Allows to print the results with the different scales. The values are as follows:
ENFORCESCALE = 0
the scales will be not changed according with the results; this allows to print the results from different files in the same scales.
ENFORCESCALE = 1
the maximum and minimum values for the used scales will be taken from the file of results, and the printing will be done according with these values.
Integer USELINESTYLES  To use (or not) different line styles for plotting. The values are as follows:
USELINESTYLES = 0
all the lines will be solid.
USELINESTYLES = 1
five different (standard) styles of lines will be used: Solid, Dash-Dash, Dot-Dot, Dash-Dot, Dash-Dot-Dot.
Integer NUMBERLINES  To put the numbers (or not) on the graphs. The values are as follows:
NUMBERLINES = 0
no numbering of the graphs.
NUMBERLINES = 1
each graph will have its number for better recognition.
Integer PRTPARAMS  To print (or not) the set of parameters used for calculations. The values are as follows:
PRTPARAMS = 0
no printing of parameters.
PRTPARAMS = 1
the set of parameters will be printed.

"""
