def setfullviewscale(scale=None, ltval=None, rbval=None, adjust=None, axisplace=None, axisvalue=None, gridcalctype=None, gridstep=None, gridminlines=None, shownum=None, ltpos=None, inpos=None, rbpos=None, ltplaces=None, inplaces=None, rbplaces=None, **kwds):
    """
Use this API to specify the parameters of the scales used for plotting the results of PV and QV analysis.

Python syntax:

setfullviewscale(scale, ltval, rbval, adjust, axisplace, axisvalue, gridcalctype, gridstep, gridminlines, shownum, ltpos, inpos, rbpos, ltplaces, inplaces, rbplaces)

where:

Integer SCALE  Is the number of the scale. The values are as follows:
SCALE = 0 QV analysis, horizontal scale for Q(V) plot.
SCALE = 1 QV analysis, vertical scale for Q(V) plot.
SCALE = 2 QV analysis, vertical scale for mismatch plot.
SCALE = 3 PV analysis, horizontal scale for incremental transfer.
SCALE = 4 PV analysis, horizontal scale for interface MW flow (bus voltage against interface flow).
SCALE = 5 PV analysis, vertical scale for bus voltage.
SCALE = 6 PV analysis, vertical scale for generator MW.
SCALE = 7 PV analysis, vertical scale for branch MVA flow.
SCALE = 8 PV analysis, vertical scale for interface MW flow.
SCALE = 9 PV analysis, vertical scale for bus voltage (bus voltage against interface flow).
Real LTVAL  Left value (for horizontal scale) or top value (for vertical scale).
Real RBVAL  Right value (for horizontal scale) or bottom value (for vertical scale).
Integer ADJUST(2)  Is an array of two elements. The values are as follows:
ADJUST(1) to adjust (or not) the left (top) value of the scale.
ADJUST(2) to adjust (or not) the right (bottom) value of the scale.
Integer AXISPLACE  Is the place of the axis. The values are as follows:
AXISPLACE = 0 on the left (top) border.
AXISPLACE = 1 the axis place is set in AXISVALUE.
AXISPLACE = 2 on the right (bottom) border.
AXISPLACE = 3 undefined, the exact value will be calculated.
Real AXISVALUE  Is the place of the axis. Valid only in case AXISPLACE = 1.
Integer GRIDCALCTYPE  The way the grid is calculated. The values are as follows:
GRIDCALCTYPE = 0
grid step is set in GRIDSTEP.
GRIDCALCTYPE = 1
grid is defined by minimum grid lines set in GRIDMINLINES.
Real GRIDSTEP  Step of the grid. Valid only in case GRIDCALCTYPE = 0.
Integer GRIDMINLINES  Minimum number of the grid lines.
Valid only in case GRIDCALCTYPE = 1.
Integer SHOWNUM(3)  Is an array of three elements. The values are as follows:
SHOWNUM (1) to show (or not) the left (top) value of the scale.
SHOWNUM (2) to show (or not) all the intermediate values for the grid.
SHOWNUM (3) to show (or not) the right (bottom) value of the scale.
Integer LTPOS  Is the place of the left (top) value relative to the left (top) border. The values are as follows:
LTPOS = 0 to the left of the border (above the border).
LTPOS = 1 centered to the border.
LTPOS = 2 to the right of the border (below the border).
Integer INPOS  Is the place of the intermediate values relative to the intermediate grid lines. The values are as follows:
INPOS = 0 to the left of the line (above the line).
INPOS = 1 centered to the line.
INPOS = 2 to the right of the line (below the line).
Integer RBPOS  Is the place of the right (bottom) value relative to the right (bottom) border. The values are as follows:
RBPOS = 0 to the left of the border (above the border).
RBPOS = 1 centered to the border.
RBPOS = 2 to the right of the border (below the border).
Integer LTPLACES  Number of digits to the right of the decimal point for the left (top) value.
Integer INPLACES  Number of digits to the right of the decimal point for intermediate values.
Integer RBPLACES  Number of digits to the right of the decimal point for the right (bottom) value.

"""
    if scale == None:
        scale = _i
    if ltval == None:
        ltval = _f
    if rbval == None:
        rbval = _f
    adjust = _makeValidListArg(adjust, _i, 2)
    if axisplace == None:
        axisplace = _i
    if axisvalue == None:
        axisvalue = _f
    if gridcalctype == None:
        gridcalctype = _i
    if gridstep == None:
        gridstep = _f
    if gridminlines == None:
        gridminlines = _i
    shownum = _makeValidListArg(shownum, _i, 3)
    if ltpos == None:
        ltpos = _i
    if inpos == None:
        inpos = _i
    if rbpos == None:
        rbpos = _i
    if ltplaces == None:
        ltplaces = _i
    if inplaces == None:
        inplaces = _i
    if rbplaces == None:
        rbplaces = _i
    arrayinfomap = {}
    arrayinfomap.update(dict([('adjust' + str(idx + 1), [adjust, idx]) for idx in range(2)]))
    arrayinfomap.update(dict([('shownum' + str(idx + 1), [shownum, idx]) for idx in range(3)]))
    _updateArgs(arrayinfomap, kwds)
    retval = psspyc.setfullviewscale(scale, ltval, rbval, adjust, axisplace, axisvalue, gridcalctype, gridstep, gridminlines, shownum, ltpos, inpos, rbpos, ltplaces, inplaces, rbplaces)
    return retval


